[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Set Wallpaper
Comment=Pick a wallpaper and how it is displayed
Exec=mb-wallpaper-picker
Icon=mb-wallpaper-picker
Terminal=false
Categories=Settings
X-Piko-Settings-Group=Display
X-Piko-NoDesktop=true
# The last two lines are read by two different programs, neither of which
# is this file's own launcher:
#
#   X-Piko-Settings-Group -- piko-settings files this under its "Display"
#     heading. Absent, the entry would still be listed, under "Other".
#   X-Piko-NoDesktop      -- matchbox-desktop-classic's modules/dotdesktop.c
#     leaves it off the desktop icon view. It is reachable from the
#     Settings window and from the panel menu; a third copy on the desktop
#     only pushes the actual applications further down a flat list.
#
# Categories=Settings still does what it always did -- it is what puts this
# in the panel menu's "Desktop Preferences" folder -- and now also what
# makes piko-settings pick the entry up at all. Do not change it without
# reading both consumers first.
